"""HSK 5 readings 9–12 and three-person soup banter: remove app-like cautions."""
import sys
from advanced_reading_repair import apply
EDITS={
9:{'-paired-reading':{
6:('我们把两个需要都告诉她。她拿出本子记下来，说下一本书名放在这周消息的最后，下周的时间和地点仍然一起发。朋友说这样就能先去借书，我也不用一条条找日期。她问我们愿不愿意帮忙看一下消息清不清楚，我们答应了。下一周收到时，朋友马上回她书已经借到，我把日期放进日历，还在旁边记了小厅的位置。',"We told her both needs. She noted them: the next title would go at the end of this week's message; next week's time and place would still arrive together. My friend could borrow the book early, and I could find the date easily. We agreed to check whether the message was clear. The following week he replied that he'd borrowed it; I added the date and small hall to my calendar.")}},
10:{'-paired-reading':{
5:('我后来写给负责人的意见很短：周四有课，八点半才结束，能不能以后考虑别的晚间。我也问了五位同学，有两位愿意周二来，一位星期三方便，另外两位说最近没有时间。负责人回信谢谢我，说会把这些安排和其他反馈放在一起看。我把五个人的回答原样发过去，没有再替没问过的同学填一个时间。',"My note to the organiser was brief: Thursday class ended at 8:30; could another evening be considered later? I asked five classmates too. Two preferred Tuesday, one Wednesday and two had no time recently. The organiser thanked me and would consider these alongside other feedback. I sent their answers as given, leaving out classmates I hadn't asked.")}},
11:{'-d':{
5:('对，平时就这么说。你还没尝呢，先喝一口。',"Yes, that's how we usually talk. You haven't tried it yet—have a sip first."),
7:('没生气，是汤太咸。我还等着他做别的菜呢。',"I'm not angry—the soup's too salty. I'm still waiting for his other dishes."),
8:('那就好。不过别叫我傻，我不喜欢。',"Good. But don't call me silly; I don't like it.")},
'-r':{
1:('我抬头问他是在夸我吗，他笑着说自己的嘴今天不用再吃别的盐了。我低头又尝一小口，确实咸得喝不下去。刚才电话一来，我把盐罐放在手边，挂了以后又拿起来，连自己都忘了前面已经放过。朋友还等着我做别的菜，我就请他先把水递来，别光站在那里看我笑。',"I asked whether that was praise. He laughed that his mouth needed no more salt today. Another tiny sip was too salty to drink. When the phone rang I'd set the salt jar beside me, then picked it up again afterwards, forgetting the first addition. Since he was waiting for the other dishes, I asked him to pass the water instead of just standing there laughing."),
2:('第一次来的朋友没有笑。她后来悄悄问，我们是不是已经开始吵架。我愣了一下，说没有，他平时就这么说，还问她刚才有没有尝。她说没有，一进门就看见我们对着汤说话。我把经过讲给她，她才明白为什么他拿盐开玩笑，不过还是先问我这汤真的能喝吗。我说等一下，马上救回来。',"The new friend didn't laugh. Quietly she asked if we'd started arguing. Taken aback, I said no and asked if she'd tasted it yet. She hadn't; she'd arrived to find us talking over the soup. Once I explained the salt, she understood the joke, but still wanted to know if it was drinkable. Wait a moment, I said—I'd rescue it."),
3:('她说自己不喜欢被叫作傻，我马上答应不这样叫。朋友也说刚才是在说我放盐，不是在说她。她点点头，问有没有能帮忙的。我让她把桌上三双筷子摆好，自己去厨房拿水。回来的时候，桌子已经收得很干净，她还把我忘在椅子上的外套挂起来。我说谢谢，这回可不是反话。',"She said she didn't like being called silly, and I agreed not to call her that. My friend explained he'd meant my salt mistake. She nodded and offered to help. I asked her to set out three pairs of chopsticks while I fetched water. When I returned, the table was tidy and she'd hung up the coat I'd left on a chair. I thanked her—and this time it wasn't irony."),
5:('后来我自己说，拿三个碗就行，这次不用替盐拿一个。大家笑了一下，也就接着吃饭。加过水的汤终于能喝了，我先给新朋友盛了一点，请她再尝尝。她说好多了，又问我平时是不是也一边接电话一边做饭。我赶紧把手机放到另一边，说今天到吃完以前，谁打来都先等一下。',"I told him to bring three bowls—no extra one for the salt. We laughed and started dinner. With water added, the soup was finally drinkable, so I served the new friend a little. Much better, she said: did I usually cook while answering calls? I put my phone aside. Whoever called could wait until we'd finished eating."),
7:('饭快吃完，雨还没停。朋友拿着伞站在门口，又看了看窗外，说今天的公园只好留到下次了。新朋友问那下次是谁做汤，我们三个都笑了。我说还是我，不过先把电话关掉。他说好，还把碗送进厨房。她回家以后发消息谢谢我们，说汤后来好喝，第一次见面也没那么紧张了。',"Near the end of dinner it was still raining. My friend stood by the door with an umbrella: the park would have to wait. The newcomer asked who'd make soup next time, and all three of us laughed. Me again, I said, but with the phone off. He agreed and took the bowls to the kitchen. Later she messaged her thanks: the soup had turned out well, and she'd felt less nervous about meeting us.")},
'-paired-reading':{
1:('我先没有插话，后来悄悄问他们是不是在吵架。朋友把前面放了两次盐的事讲给我，又解释后面那句今天不用吃别的盐。我这才明白，自己一进门没看到做饭，连汤都还没尝，难怪听不懂。他把杯子递给我，说先喝水，汤还得等一会儿。我坐下来，听他们商量加多少水，心里慢慢放松。',"I didn't interrupt at first, then quietly asked whether they were arguing. My friend explained the two salt additions and the joke about needing no more salt. I'd arrived too late to see the cooking and hadn't tasted it. He handed me a cup of water while the soup was fixed. Listening to them discuss how much water to add, I gradually relaxed."),
2:('我告诉他们，不喜欢有人叫我傻。以前有人这样叫，我说不喜欢，他还是继续，后来我就不太想去那个聚会。这次朋友马上说好，不这样叫，还请我帮忙摆筷子。我打开旁边的抽屉，找到三双放在桌上。他问我碗在哪里，我指了指他身后的柜子，终于也能在他们说话的时候接上一句。',"I told them I disliked being called silly. Someone at another gathering had kept doing it even after I'd asked, and I'd stopped wanting to go. Here my friend immediately agreed and asked me to set out chopsticks. I found three pairs in a drawer. Asked where the bowls were, I pointed to the cupboard behind him; finally I could join in their conversation."),
3:('后来做汤的人也说别再说了。我原来以为他们很熟，就一直这样笑着讲，可他放下水的时候，已经不像刚才那么轻松。另一个人又补一句，他认真问怎么还来。我赶紧把刚摆好的筷子往旁边挪，给碗留出地方。那个人道歉以后去拿碗，回来没有再讲盐，问的是我们每个人要多少汤。',"Later the cook asked him to stop. I'd thought close friends would keep joking, but when he set down the water he looked less relaxed. One more remark drew a serious question: why another? I moved the chopsticks aside to make room for bowls. After apologising, the friend fetched them; returning, he asked how much soup we each wanted."),
4:('拿碗以后，做汤的人自己说这次不用替盐拿一个，大家才又笑起来。他把一勺汤放进我的碗，我先尝了一口，说现在好多了。刚才去拿碗的朋友问我敢不敢多喝，我说可以啊，又把碗往前送了送。这次我听懂了前面的事，也知道他们已经换了话题，不用坐在那里猜到底该不该笑。',"When the bowls arrived, the cook joked that the salt didn't need its own bowl, and we laughed again. I tasted a spoonful and said it was better. Would I dare have more? Of course; I pushed my bowl forward. Now I understood what had happened and could hear the topic moving on, instead of sitting there wondering whether to laugh."),
7:('回家以后，我给朋友发了一条谢谢，说汤后来好了，聊天也让我放松。他回我，下次天气好就去公园，今天说的那本书也会带上。我问是不是还要自己带碗，他发来一个笑脸，说不用，公园没有那道汤。我这次看见消息就笑了，想起我们刚才在门口说的话，把下次的日期先记在日历里。',"At home I thanked my friend: the soup had turned out well and the chat had helped me relax. Next time in good weather we'd go to the park, and he'd bring the book we'd discussed. Did I need my own bowl? He sent a smile: no, there'd be no soup in the park. This time I laughed at once, remembering our doorway conversation, and added the next date to my calendar.")}},
12:{'-paired-reading':{
2:('我先把歌词朗读了一遍，不跟音乐，听清楚把旧信收进盒里后面还有不是把名字忘记。我指给朋友看，说刚才车上真把收信听成了关灯。她把视频往前拖了一点，桌上的灯一直亮着。我又读了一遍，想到的是把东西放好以后，仍然舍不得走；她说自己倒是先注意到后面开窗。我们把两个地方都找出来，轮流看了一次。',"I read the lyrics without music and caught the line after putting the old letters in a box: it wasn't forgetting the name. On the bus I'd really heard putting away letters as turning off the light. My friend dragged the video back—the lamp stayed on. I still felt the character was reluctant to leave after tidying. She'd noticed the later window opening first. We found both moments and watched them in turn.")}}
}
EDITS[12]['-paired-reading'][7]=('我把完整视频发给另一位朋友，说看完再告诉我最喜欢哪一段。她晚上回我，先说那个开窗的动作，又问我为什么一直在讲灯。我把刚才漏听的两句发过去，她说原来收的是信，不是把灯关掉。第二天见面，我们又把短版打开，对着时间找少掉的那几秒。她喜欢后半段的声音，我更注意角色回头的地方，两个人各把自己喜欢的那一段放了一遍。最后她把歌名存好，说下次坐车也要听，我提醒她别学我把一句话听成另一句。',"I sent a friend the full video and asked for her favourite part. That evening she mentioned the window opening and wondered why I kept talking about the lamp. I sent the two lines I'd missed: so the letters were put away, not the light switched off. Next day we compared the short version and found the missing seconds. She liked the sound in the second half; I noticed the character turning back. We each replayed our favourite section. Saving the song title for her next bus ride, she laughed when I warned her not to mishear it as I had.")

apply(5,EDITS,'Three-person soup dialogue keeps distinct speaker IDs but loses the blanket skill judgment and consent explanation. Readings show initial confusion, an actual request to stop, apology, the cook’s own bowl joke and sincere enjoyment at home. Newcomer still asks not to be called 傻; no universal irony rule is taught. Interview/weekly notice and five-classmate survey remain evidence-bound text types. Short/full video distinction and misheard light/letters facts retained. Native flags: 汤救回来, salt-bowl comeback, X什么X strength and friendly mainland banter.',glosses=[('盐罐','salt jar'),('愣','be momentarily taken aback'),('盛','serve; ladle food'),('抽屉','drawer'),('柜子','cupboard; cabinet'),('一勺','one spoonful'),('挪','move something a little'),('笑脸','smiling face'),('反话','ironic remark'),('反馈','feedback')],publish='--publish' in sys.argv)
